</table> <p style="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt; font-family:ARIAL" id="toc30002_16"><span style="color:#430098"><span style="font-weight:bold">Board Skills </span></span></p> <p style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt; font-family:ARIAL">The following Director Skills Matrix highlights the mix of key skills and experiences of the nominees that, among other factors, led the Board and the Nominating&#160;&amp; Governance Committee to recommend these nominees for election to the Board. The Director Skills Matrix is intended to depict notable areas of focus for each director based on the current composition of the Board, and not having a mark does not mean that a particular director does not possess that qualification or skill. Nominees have developed competencies in these skills through education, direct experience, and oversight responsibilities. The demographic information presented below is based on voluntary self-identification by each nominee. Additional biographical information on each nominee is set out below. </p> <p style="font-size:12pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&#160;</p>
