<td style="vertical-align:top;text-align:left"><div style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-family: ARIAL; font-size: 9pt; text-align: left; line-height: normal;"><ix:nonNumeric name="ecd:MeasureName" contextRef="P01_01_2025To12_31_2025_5TypedMemberecdMeasureAxis" id="ixv-14636">Total Shareholder Return</ix:nonNumeric> </div></td></tr></table></ix:nonNumeric> <div style="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt; font-family:ARIAL">These performance measures influence how we set our executive compensation levels, determine incentive plan payout decisions, and impact the value of the Company, which in turn is reflected in the compensation paid to our PEOs and the Other NEOs. </div><div id="toc30002_51" style="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt; font-family:ARIAL"><div style="color: rgb(67, 0, 152); letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;"><div style="display:inline;"><div style="font-weight:bolder;display:inline;">Relationship Between Compensation Actually Paid and Performance Measures </div></div></div></div><div style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt; font-family:ARIAL">The Pay Versus Performance table above and the charts below demonstrate that the compensation actually paid to our PEOs and the Other NEOs was generally aligned with our performance based on the performance measures presented in the table over the covered fiscal years, including TSR, net income, and Adjusted EBITDA. </div><div style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt ; font-size:8pt">&#160;</div>
